{number: 68}
{title: Just As I Am, without One Plea}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Just as I am, without one plea,
But that Thy [G7] blood was shed for [C] me,
And that Thou [F] bidd'st me come to Thee,
O Lamb of [C] God, I [G7] come, I [C] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Just as I am, and waiting not
To rid my [G7] soul of one dark [C] blot,
To Thee whose [F] blood can cleanse each spot,
O Lamb of [C] God, I [G7] come, I [C] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Just as I am, though tossed about
With many a [G7] conflict, many a [C] doubt,
Fightings and [F] fears within, without,
O Lamb of [C] God, I [G7] come, I [C] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Just as I am, Thou wilt receive,
Wilt welcome, [G7] pardon, cleanse, re-[C] lieve;
Because Thy [F] promise I believe,
O Lamb of [C] God, I [G7] come, I [C] come.
{end_of_verse}
